# MultiBand 6 ESP32 Atomic Beacon — Licensing & Terms

Copyright (c) 2026 Robert Longbottom (@thomaslr)

This project uses a dual reciprocal copyleft licensing structure for software and hardware, keeping the project open and free for makers, hobbyists, and open-source/open-hardware builders while preventing closed-source commercial appropriation:

---

## 1. Software & Firmware: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPLv3)

All software source code in this repository — including the Rust firmware (`firmware-rust/`), embedded web interface assets (`data/`), web installer (`docs/`), and build/CI tooling (`.github/`) — is licensed under the **GNU General Public License Version 3** (**GPLv3**, SPDX: `GPL-3.0-only`).

* **Permissions:** Anyone may study, modify, run, and distribute the software (for personal, educational, or commercial purposes) under the terms of the GPLv3.
* **Reciprocal Copyleft:** Any distributed binary, modified version, or derivative software must be licensed under the GPLv3 and accompanied by its complete corresponding source code.
* **Full License Text:** See [`LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt`](LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt).

---

## 2. Hardware, PCB & Enclosure Designs: CERN Open Hardware Licence v2 — Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S v2)

All hardware and mechanical design files in this repository — including KiCad schematics, PCB layouts, layout generator scripts (`make_pcb.py`), Gerber/drill manufacturing archives, Bills of Materials (`bom.csv`), pick-and-place centroid files (`positions.csv`), and breadboard documentation in `pcb/`, as well as parametric OpenSCAD sources (`.scad`) and 3D-printable STL models in `enclosure/` — are licensed under the **CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal** (**CERN-OHL-S v2**, SPDX: `CERN-OHL-S-2.0`).

* **Permissions:** Anyone may study, modify, manufacture, assemble, and distribute hardware products based on these designs (for personal, educational, or commercial purposes) under the terms of the CERN-OHL-S v2.
* **Reciprocal Copyleft:** If you convey or distribute physical hardware products or design files based on these designs (whether unmodified or modified/derivative), you must make the Complete Source (schematics, PCB layouts, CAD files, scripts, BOMs, and documentation) available under the CERN-OHL-S v2 and preserve all required notices.
* **Full License Text:** See [`LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-v2.txt`](LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-v2.txt).

---

## 3. Commercial License Available

If you or your organization wish to manufacture, sell pre-assembled devices or kits, redistribute, or integrate this design (firmware, hardware, enclosure, or derivatives) into a proprietary or closed-source commercial product without being subject to the reciprocal copyleft source-sharing requirements of the **GPLv3** or **CERN-OHL-S v2**, a separate commercial license is available directly from the copyright holder.

For commercial licensing inquiries, OEM/bulk manufacturing rights, or custom hardware engineering:
* **Contact:** Robert Longbottom via GitHub [@thomaslr](https://github.com/thomaslr)

